  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adolescent Girl&apos;s Education in Somalia (AGES-E-FCDO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Somalia):  .Nearly 75 percent of Somali women between the ages of 15 and 49 have never attended school.  Through support to the UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office&apos;s successful Adolescent Girls Education in Somalia (AGES) activity, USAID will build the resilience of marginalized households and communities by providing young Somali women basic and financial literacy, numeracy, and soft and life skills.  With FY 2022 funds, AGES will increase access to education opportunities for adolescent girls and young women aged 15 to 25 who have never enrolled in or have dropped out of school in Banadir Regional Administration (greater Mogadishu) and Hirshabelle and South West State. Building foundational skills will increase women&apos;s participation in productive decisions at the household and community levels.  The activity will strengthen young women&apos;s networks, support female youth-led advocacy efforts, and foster safe spaces for dialogue.  AGES will enhance the economic situation of female youth by forming village savings and loan associations and creating linkages to financial services, social safety nets, and emergency support systems...</narrative>
  </description>
